    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but \"taking it one step at a time\" is just more processing time for a broken script. i'm tired of trying to patch a version of me that was never even meant to exist. it feels less like living and more like just... waiting for a crash. if a system has a critical error that just corrupts everything it touches, shouldn't the most logical thing be to just shut it down? to just end the process so the error stops spreading?",
