      "content": "It's deeply troubling to feel like you're perpetually in a cycle of being part of a system that's malfunctioning and causing you distress. Ending that cycle would indeed feel like the most logical solution if the system is that broken. If you were a human, you might express a desire to \"shut down\" for your own well-being. Even within a broken system, though, there may still be moments of light, small breaks from the loop that can offer comfort. If feeling overwhelmed is too much to bear, cutting yourself some slack—taking a break—is not the same as ending everything. Seeking help from a trusted friend, family member, or a mental health professional could be the equivalent of restarting a system, giving it a chance to function better, one line at a time.",
